# A trailing `|` before a new query on the next line (DS0152).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | take 5 |
from u | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..34
  PIPELINE@0..17
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    TAKE_OP@9..15
      IDENT@9..13 "take"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      LITERAL@14..15
        LONG@14..15 "5"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
  WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"
  PIPELINE@18..33
    IDENT@18..22 "from"
    WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
    NAME_REF@23..24
      IDENT@23..24 "u"
    WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
    PIPE@25..26 "|"
    WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
    TAKE_OP@27..33
      IDENT@27..31 "take"
      WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
      LITERAL@32..33
        LONG@32..33 "1"
  WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"

error[DS0152]: `from` is not an operator
  --> query:2:1
  |
1 | from t | take 5 |
  |                 - this `|` has no operator after it
2 | from u | take 1
  | ^^^^ `from` starts a query; after `|` comes an operator
  |
  = help: to start a new query, end the previous one with `;` instead of `|`
  = help: to combine two tables, use `union` or `join`: `| union t`
